y  again you buy it once  and then you get a management company to  put a tenant in there and if the tenant  moves out the management company finds  another tenant  and you the owner just get paid  so i get paid every single month i spend  less than five  minutes a month managing my property  portfolio  and my management companies manage all  the tenants deal with everything  they take all the money minus their  management costs and then  i get the profit every single month that  happens that's going to continue  happening  happening not just all my life but my  kids life  my grandkids life they're gonna keep  getting rent off my properties  you cannot say that is not passive  income  the only way that property is not  passive is if you've set it up whereby  it's not systemized  very easy to systemize so that's number  one  number two is business people say  passive income doesn't exist  why is it then that every single  business by its very definition  is set up to create passive income you  might say what are you talking about  samuel  well a business is not a business unless  you have  staff you have customers and you have  processes  so the processes and the idea of  business is so that it functions  without you and if you've got a business  that's functioning without you  what does that give you that gives you  passive income  and most businesses that are set up  properly  are set up to create ultimately passive  income so that's number two  traditional business number three is  online businesses  now the difference between an online  business and a traditional business  is for an online business you don't even  need staff  i've seen individuals making millions of  pounds  with an online business with  subscription  and they don't even have hardly any or  any staff at all  so online businesses like subscriptions  this is a great way  to get passive income lastly number four  and you can't  argue with this and this that is  royalties  i've written several books 